# benchspec credentials — copy to `.env` and fill in what you need.
# `.env` is gitignored; benchspec loads it before pytest collects anything.
# `GEMINI_API_KEY` is required for every graded run under the default binder.
# Other credentials depend on the task and judge harnesses you select — or set
# `provider = "openrouter"` on the binder, the judge, and the arms, and the whole
# run needs only OPENROUTER_API_KEY.
#
# This repo's own `make e2e` needs four: GEMINI_API_KEY, a Claude credential
# (CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY) for the arms, OPENAI_API_KEY for
# the Codex judge, and OPENROUTER_API_KEY for its second run, which puts the
# binder, the judge, and every harness on OpenRouter.

# --- Binder (required for every graded run unless it is on OpenRouter) ---
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# --- Claude Code harness (and the default judge) ---
# Prefer the OAuth token from `claude setup-token` for subscription-backed auth;
# otherwise set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. Set one.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- OpenRouter (any component with `provider = "openrouter"`) ---
# The one key a run needs when the binder, the judge, and every arm are set to
# `openrouter`; also `make e2e`'s second run. Under the default provider it is
# OpenCode's preferred credential.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- OpenCode harness ---
# Any one provider credential is enough for an OpenCode arm under the default
# provider: OPENROUTER_API_KEY above, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, or a Gemini key. The
# binder's GEMINI_API_KEY is injected to the SDK's expected
# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY automatically.

# --- Codex harness (also the judge in this repo's `make e2e`) ---
# Set one: OPENAI_API_KEY or CODEX_API_KEY (OpenAI API), CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN
# (ChatGPT subscription), or CODEX_AUTH_JSON_PATH pointing at a Codex CLI auth.json.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
CODEX_API_KEY=
CODEX_ACCESS_TOKEN=
CODEX_AUTH_JSON_PATH=

# --- Optional overrides ---
# Trigger-routing harness; output-eval arms use their configured harnesses.
# BENCHSPEC_AGENT=claude-code
# Pin sandbox task-harness CLI versions instead of "latest".
# BENCHSPEC_CODEX_VERSION=latest
# BENCHSPEC_OPENCODE_VERSION=latest
